* CUPC/8 behavioural power models (ngspice).
*
* These are NOT vendor models. Advanced Monolithic Systems, Richtek and
* Silergy publish none for the AMS1117, RT9013 and SY6280. Each model is built
* from the datasheet figures that hw/power/design.py passes in as parameters,
* and is only as good as those figures. The vendor models (TI TLV62569,
* TLV7011) are fetched by hw/power/models/fetch.py.

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* LDO_BEH: a linear regulator as a Thevenin source.
*
*   ideal source  VSET, ramped up over TSS from t = 0, plus the input
*                 ripple shaped by the PSRR: PSRR_DC below F_PSRR, rising
*                 20 dB/decade above it, up to 0 dB (no loop gain left)
*   clamped by    dropout: never above VIN - (DROP0 + RDROP * Iout)
*                 current limit: collapses above ILIM
*   behind        the closed-loop output impedance RDC + (LEQ || RP): RDC is
*                 the load regulation, LEQ the rise in impedance as the loop
*                 gain falls, RP the pass device's own impedance at high
*                 frequency. LEQ and RP are fitted to a datasheet load-step
*                 figure (see design.py).
*   input         draws Iout + IQ from IN
*
* Limits: it has no loop, so it says nothing about stability with a given
* output capacitor; and it can sink current, which a real pass device can't
* (this flatters the overshoot on load release, so the checks use the droop
* when load is applied).
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt LDO_BEH in out gnd params: VSET=3.3 TSS=100u DROP0=1 RDROP=0.2 ILIM=1
+ IQ=5m PSRR_DC=1e-3 F_PSRR=1k VIN_NOM=5 RDC=5m LEQ=0.3u RP=0.2
* PSRR: PSRR_DC * (vin - VIN_NOM), plus a first-order high-pass of vin with
* its corner where the rising PSRR reaches 0 dB (F_PSRR / PSRR_DC)
Chp in hp {1 / (6.2832 * 1000 * F_PSRR / PSRR_DC)}
Rhp hp gnd 1k
Bps ps gnd v = {PSRR_DC} * (v(in, gnd) - {VIN_NOM}) + (1 - {PSRR_DC}) * v(hp, gnd)
* the source, clamped by dropout and current limit
Bsrc src gnd v = max(0, min({VSET} * min(1, time / {TSS}) + v(ps, gnd),
+   v(in, gnd) - {DROP0} - {RDROP} * max(0, i(Vsense)))
+   - 100 * max(0, i(Vsense) - {ILIM}))
Rdc src z {RDC}
Leq z o2 {LEQ}
Rp z o2 {RP}
Vsense o2 out 0
* input current
Bin in gnd i = max(0, i(Vsense)) + {IQ}
.ends LDO_BEH

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* SW_BEH: a current-limited, soft-started load switch or eFuse (the input TPS25947).
*
*   TDLY after t = 0 (IN is applied at t = 0 in every deck) the gate ramps,
*   and the output follows it from 0 to IN over TON (SY6280: 120 us). The
*   channel is RON when fully on. Above ILIM the switch holds its current at
*   ILIM (the SY6280 limits; it does not latch off). Reverse current is blocked (the SY6280 has no body diode).
*   Thermal shutdown is not modelled: the inrush check computes the energy.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt SW_BEH in out gnd params: RON=80m ILIM=1.5 TON=120u TDLY=5u
* channel: i = x / RON, limited to ILIM with a sharp but smooth knee (the
* 8-norm: within 5% of the linear value up to 0.9 * ILIM)
Bx x gnd v = max(0, v(in, gnd) * min(1, max(0, time - {TDLY}) / {TON}) - v(out, gnd)) / {RON} / {ILIM}
Bch in out i = {ILIM} * v(x, gnd) / pow(1 + pow(v(x, gnd), 8), 0.125)
.ends SW_BEH

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BB_BEH: a buck-boost converter (TPS63802 class) as a Thevenin source.
*
*   Used because TI's TPS63802 PSpice model does not run in ngspice-47 (see
*   hw/power/boost.py). A buck-boost regulates whether its input is above or
*   below its output, so: an ideal source VSET, ramped over TSS, behind the
*   closed-loop output impedance RDC + (LEQ || RP), fitted to the datasheet's
*   load-transient figure. It shuts down (source to 0) while IN is below
*   VINMIN or above VOVP (input over-voltage). Its input draws the output
*   power over ETA, plus IQ. No ripple: the checks add the datasheet's
*   power-save ripple band themselves.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt BB_BEH in out gnd params: VSET=5 TSS=500u ETA=0.85 IQ=11u VINMIN=1.3 VOVP=5.7
+ RDC=5m LEQ=1u RP=0.2
* on between VINMIN and VOVP through smooth steps: 50 mV wide at VINMIN (a
* hard switch stalls ngspice as the input rises through it), 5 mV at VOVP (so
* an input 90 mV under the OVP is fully on)
Bsrc src gnd v = {VSET} * min(1, time / {TSS}) * 0.5 * (1 + tanh((v(in, gnd) - {VINMIN}) / 0.05))
+   * 0.5 * (1 + tanh(({VOVP} - v(in, gnd)) / 0.005))
Rdc src z {RDC}
Leq z o2 {LEQ}
Rp z o2 {RP}
Vsense o2 out 0
Bin in gnd i = max(0, v(out, gnd) * i(Vsense)) / ({ETA} * max(v(in, gnd), 0.5)) + {IQ}
.ends BB_BEH
